@metmuseum

@TheShardsFX may be set in 1981, but the wardrobe feels refreshingly modern. #FXPartner. This is due in part to the fact that the beginning of a new decade is rarely aesthetically cohesive. Instead, it’s a transitional moment when the styles of one era overlap with those of the next—in this case, the late ‘70s, New Wave, and, of course, the emerging aesthetic of the ‘80s. What also makes the wardrobe feel so contemporary is its embrace of preppy style, which is currently experiencing yet another resurgence.

Though preppy style has long been part of the fashion vernacular, the publication of The Official Preppy Handbook in 1980 made the rules governing the subculture visible to a wider audience. More than forty years later, the book feels just as relevant today as it was when it was published. What both The Shards and the book ultimately illustrate is that preppy style has endured because it’s built on the very best versions of timeless wardrobe staples—pieces that look good on just about everyone.

To see just how well it holds up, we sourced both vintage and contemporary pieces that showcase the breadth of the aesthetic while offering inspiration for recreating the look yourself.

@TheShardsFX is now streaming on Hulu.

